  "articleBody": "Tearing out an outdated shower sounds simple until you uncover rotted framing or damp subfloors behind the backer board. In older homes across the Denver metro area, persistent humidity and minor grout cracking often hide slow-draining leaks that work their way into adjacent spaces before showing visible warning signs.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process:\nWhen we remove a failing enclosure, we follow a systematic approach to protect your home:\n- Isolating and shutting down supply lines cleanly so adjacent fixtures remain unaffected.\n- Protecting hallways, vanity finishes, and floors from heavy tile shards and drywall dust.\n- Carefully cutting through surround panels without slicing concealed electrical lines or vent stacks.\n- Inspecting wood studs, plates, and subfloor sheathing for fungal growth or softened timber.\n- Evaluating the existing trap, drain assembly, and rough-in plumbing to see if upgrades are needed.\n\nWhen to Call a Professional:\nIf you notice spongy flooring near the curb, musty odors, or signs of mold, structural repairs may be necessary before new work begins. Abraham Becerra and the team at HH Remodeling LLC handle everything from demolition and framing repair to tile work. Call us at 303-505-0866 to discuss your tear-out.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
